WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:15.840
A product ID such as GTIN, UPC, EAN, JAN, or ISBN, helps to provide fast and accurate product identification,

00:00:15.840 --> 00:00:20.978
streamlines inventory management, and reduces errors through barcode scanning.

00:00:20.978 --> 00:00:22.120
However, some

00:00:22.120 --> 00:00:27.206
products do not require a product ID in order to be sold in the Amazon store.

00:00:27.206 --> 00:00:28.160
To list a

00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:34.800
product without a product ID, you'll need to apply for a GTIN exemption during the listing process.

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:41.760
To determine if your product is eligible for GTIN exemption, start by making sure it is not

00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:44.240
already being sold in the Amazon catalog.

00:00:44.240 --> 00:00:49.200
It does not have a product ID or GS1 barcode and that you

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:52.918
have approval to sell in that product's category if required.

00:00:52.918 --> 00:00:55.520
Next, check to make sure that your

00:00:55.520 --> 00:01:00.976
product falls into one of the categories that allows GTIN exemptions.

00:01:00.976 --> 00:01:02.960
These include private label

00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:08.800
or handmade products, products that you manufacture, brand, or publish without barcodes,

00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:15.680
parts without a product ID, for example auto parts or mobile accessories, bundled products,

00:01:15.680 --> 00:01:21.077
for example a belt or wallet pack, or generic unbranded products.

00:01:21.077 --> 00:01:23.040
To start your application,

00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:28.960
go to the Add Products page in Seller Central and enter your product title into the search bar.

00:01:29.520 --> 00:01:33.699
At the bottom of the search results, click Create a New Listing.

00:01:33.699 --> 00:01:35.440
Start by filling in your

00:01:35.440 --> 00:01:39.740
product details and select the appropriate product type and category.

00:01:39.740 --> 00:01:42.320
Then, enter a brand name for

00:01:42.320 --> 00:01:43.158
your product.

00:01:43.158 --> 00:01:49.021
If your product is generic, select this product does not have a brand name.

00:01:49.021 --> 00:01:49.440
Check

00:01:49.440 --> 00:01:53.136
this product does not have a product ID and click Next.

00:01:53.136 --> 00:01:56.160
If you are a brand owner or are selling

00:01:56.160 --> 00:01:59.440
generic products, you'll see an auto approval pop up.

00:01:59.440 --> 00:02:02.720
Your approval could take up to one hour to

00:02:02.720 --> 00:02:07.352
take effect, so feel free to save your listing as a draft and come back later.

00:02:07.352 --> 00:02:08.800
If you try to list

00:02:08.800 --> 00:02:14.960
a product from a brand that requires a product ID or if your product is a book and you check this

00:02:14.960 --> 00:02:20.490
product does not have a brand name, your GTIN exemption will be automatically declined.

00:02:20.490 --> 00:02:21.280
If you

00:02:21.280 --> 00:02:27.600
are selling a brand that does not require a product ID, you'll be prompted to apply for a GTIN

00:02:27.600 --> 00:02:28.153
exemption.

00:02:28.153 --> 00:02:33.687
You might see multiple approval required alerts during this process.

00:02:33.687 --> 00:02:34.240
However,

00:02:34.240 --> 00:02:38.394
all approvals will be processed through a single application.

00:02:38.394 --> 00:02:40.240
Make sure your application

00:02:40.240 --> 00:02:46.800
includes clear, high-quality, real-world photos of all sides of your product to reduce the chances

00:02:46.800 --> 00:02:48.625
of your application being rejected.

00:02:48.625 --> 00:02:52.640
Once your application has been submitted, it can take up to

00:02:52.640 --> 00:02:54.667
48 hours to receive a decision.

00:02:54.667 --> 00:02:58.720
You can check the status of your applications on the View Selling

00:02:58.720 --> 00:02:59.771
Applications page.

00:02:59.771 --> 00:03:06.080
You'll need to request separate GTIN exemption approvals for each product category

00:03:06.080 --> 00:03:09.299
and each Amazon store where you intend to sell.

00:03:09.299 --> 00:03:12.160
Once approved for a category in a store,

00:03:12.160 --> 00:03:17.200
you can list multiple products within that category without additional exemptions.

00:03:17.200 --> 00:03:22.480
To learn more about specific requirements for your product category or troubleshoot common

00:03:22.480 --> 00:03:28.080
errors like brand name mismatches, go to the list products that do not have a product ID

00:03:28.080 --> 00:03:34.817
help page in Seller Central.
